<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Syracuse</h1><p class="st-meta">734 BCE – 212 BCE (approx.) · capital Syracuse</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The greatest Greek city of the West, which defeated Carthage and Athens, ruled much of Sicily under its tyrants and kings, and fell to Rome in 212 BCE.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Corinthian colonists led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/archias-of-corinth">Archias</a> founded Syracuse in 734 or 733 BCE on the island of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ortygia">Ortygia</a>, with its freshwater spring of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fountain-of-arethusa">Arethusa</a> and two harbours. The city expanded onto the mainland and founded daughter colonies including <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kamarina">Kamarina</a>, controlling south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Its politics swung between aristocracy, democracy and powerful tyrants. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gelon">Gelon</a> made it the leading Greek power and with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theron-of-acragas">Theron of Acragas</a> crushed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a> at <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/himera">Himera</a> in 480 BCE. A democracy defeated the Athenian expedition in 415–413 BCE. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dionysius-i-of-syracuse">Dionysius I</a> built the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/epipolae">Epipolae</a> walls and an empire over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a> and southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/agathocles-of-syracuse">Agathocles</a> later took the title of king. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hiero-ii-of-syracuse">Hieron II</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome's</a> ally from 263 BCE, Syracuse enjoyed peace and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/archimedes">Archimedes</a> worked there.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hiero-ii-of-syracuse">Hieron II</a>'s death Syracuse sided with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marcus-claudius-marcellus">Marcus Claudius Marcellus</a> besieged it from 214 BCE and took it in 212 BCE, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/archimedes">Archimedes</a> was killed. It became the seat of the Roman governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a> and remained a major city; its ancient centre is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="city state, 734 BCE – 212 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V42 H32 V34 H40 V42 H46 V34 H54 V42 H60 V34 H68 V42 H76 V82 Z"/><path d="M44 82 V66 Q50 58 56 66 V82"/><path d="M34 54 H40 M60 54 H66"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">city state</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Italy</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:45.09%;width:10.39%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>734 BCE – 212 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/8th-century-bce">8th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>city state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Syracuse</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Gelon, Dionysius I, Hieron II</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Greek religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Doric Greek</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Syrakousai, Kingdom of Syracuse</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-473&amp;focus=syracuse" aria-label="Syracuse on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5063 843 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Syracuse lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5383 1099L5405 1060